  "description": "6280, 6281 and 6282 3 x 5m Himalayan Birch trees - 6280 and 6281 on the left-hand side to be trimmed all over reducing up to 0.6m where necessary to improve shape. The larger tree (6282) on the right-hand side to be trimmed all over reducing up to 1m where necessary to improve the shape.\r6729 Ash Tree - Remove the two lowest overhanging branches on the Tiverton Lodge side that extend over and before the shed, the cuts must be made carefully back to a suitable secondary branch union located further toward the boundary.\r6730 Japanese Pagola - Prune one low limb overhanging on the Tiverton Lodge side (approx. 3m in length) by removing it back to a suitable secondary branch union",
